ollection returns null instead of interpreting later indented text as mapping children."},{"markdown":"Deep lookups skip unrelated sibling subtrees and comments, support consistent nondefault indentation, and cannot resolve a leaf outside the selected parent.","startLine":69,"endLine":69,"text":"Deep lookups skip unrelated sibling subtrees and comments, support consistent nondefault indentation, and cannot resolve a leaf outside the selected parent."},{"markdown":"Speech-to-text IPC sends recorded desktop audio through the Hermes API server, not through the active chat model endpoint.","startLine":73,"endLine":73,"text":"Speech-to-text IPC sends recorded desktop audio through the Hermes API server, not through the active chat model endpoint."},{"markdown":"[[src/main/ipc/register.ts#registerIpcHandlers]] exposes `transcribe-audio` for the preload bridge, and [[src/main/hermes.ts#transcribeAudio]] posts a base64 data URL to `/api/audio/transcribe`. If the local gateway lacks that desktop route, it falls back to the Python `tools.transcription_tools.transcribe_audio` dispatcher, so local Whisper, Groq, OpenAI, ElevenLabs, and command/plugin STT providers remain independent from the selected chat model.","startLine":75,"endLine":75,"text":"src/main/ipc/register.ts#registerIpcHandlers exposes transcribe-audio for the preload bridge, and src/main/hermes.ts#transcribeAudio posts a base64 data URL to /api/audio/transcribe. If the local gateway lacks that desktop route, it falls back to the Python tools.transcription_tools.transcribe_audio dispatcher, so local Whisper, Groq, OpenAI, ElevenLabs, and command/plugin STT providers remain independent from the selected chat model."},{"markdown":"Every RAZUM Desktop SSH `.env` update runs as a remote locked transaction, so overlapping provider and messaging writes preserve unrelated credentials.","startLine":79,"endLine":79,"text":"Every RAZUM Desktop SSH .env update runs as a remote locked transaction, so overlapping provider and messaging writes preserve unrelated credentials."},{"markdown":"[[src/main/ssh-remote.ts#sshSetEnvValue]] sends all mutations through [[src/main/ssh-env-update.ts#REMOTE_ENV_UPDATE_SCRIPT]]. The remote helper locks a stable sibling `.env.lock`, reads the latest file only after acquiring the lock, and replaces it atomically through a same-directory temporary file.","startLine":81,"endLine":81,"text":"src/main/ssh-remote.ts#sshSetEnvValue sends all mutations through src/main/ssh-env-update.ts#REMOTE_ENV_UPDATE_SCRIPT. The remote helper locks a stable sibling .env.lock, reads the latest file only after acquiring the lock, and replaces it atomically through a same-directory temporary file."},{"markdown":"Paths, keys, and values travel as JSON on standard input rather than credential-bearing shell arguments. Existing line endings, unrelated lines, ownership, permissions, ACLs, extended attributes, security labels, and symlink targets are preserved. A new `.env` is created with mode `0600`; unsafe metadata or filesystem failures abort the replacement.","startLine":83,"endLine":83,"text":"Paths, keys, and values travel as JSON on standard input rather than credential-bearing shell arguments. Existing line endings, unrelated lines, ownership, permissions, ACLs, extended attributes, security labels, and symlink targets are preserved. A new .env is created with mode 0600; unsafe metadata or filesystem failures abort the replacement."},{"markdown":"This lock coordinates Desktop writers across processes and connections. Manual tools and Hermes Agent do not use the Desktop lock, so they should not edit the same `.env` concurrently with a Desktop save.","startLine":85,"endLine":85,"text":"This lock coordinates Desktop writers across processes and connections. Manual tools and Hermes Agent do not use the Desktop lock, so they should not edit the same .env concurrently with a Desktop save."},{"markdown":"Independent Desktop updates wait for the same remote lock and each read the newest committed file before modifying one key.","startLine":89,"endLine":89,"text":"Independent Desktop updates wait for the same remote lock and each read the newest committed file before modifying one key."},{"markdown":"The default and named profiles resolve to separate `.env` paths, while every secret stays in the SSH process's standard input and out of its command arguments.","startLine":93,"endLine":93,"text":"The default and named profiles resolve to separate .env paths, while every secret stays in the SSH process's standard input and out of its command arguments."},{"markdown":"Read, validation, fsync, metadata, and replacement failures leave the original credential file unchanged, clean temporary files, and propagate an error to the caller.","startLine":97,"endLine":97,"text":"Read, validation, fsync, metadata, and replacement failures leave the original credential file unchanged, clean temporary files, and propagate an error to the caller."},{"markdown":"Files the agent produced on a remote Hermes server are fetched through the dashboard's managed-files API, because `/api/media` only serves images from the gateway's own media folders.","startLine":101,"endLine":101,"text":"Files the agent produced on a remote Hermes server are fetched through the dashboard's managed-files API, because /api/media only serves images from the gateway's own media folders."},{"markdown":"[[src/main/remote-files.ts#remoteDownloadFile]] streams `/api/files/download` into `<dest>.part` and renames it only after the whole body arrived, so a dropped connection never leaves a truncated document under the name the user chose. [[src/main/remote-files.ts#remoteFileExists]] probes with a one-byte range request, and [[src/main/remote-files.ts#remoteReadFile]] reads small images into memory for inline display. The save, open and exists handlers in [[src/main/ipc/register.ts]] try this machine's disk first, then this route, then `/api/media` for older servers, and show an error dialog instead of failing silently. The server hands over only files under its managed-files root, which a deployment sets with `HERMES_DASHBOARD_FILES_ROOT`.","startLine":103,"endLine":103,"text":"src/main/remote-files.ts#remoteDownloadFile streams /api/files/download into <dest>.part and renames it only after the whole body arrived, so a dropped connection never leaves a truncated document under the name the user chose. src/main/remote-files.ts#remoteFileExists probes with a one-byte range request, and src/main/remote-files.ts#remoteReadFile reads small images into memory for inline display. The save, open and exists handlers in src/main/ipc/register.ts try this machine's disk first, then this route, then /api/media for older servers, and show an error dialog instead of failing silently. The server hands over only files under its managed-files root, which a deployment sets with HERMES_DASHBOARD_FILES_ROOT."}],"blocks":[{"type":"heading","start":0,"end":14,"startLine":1,"endLine":1,"children":[]},{"type":"paragraph","start":16,"end":119,"startLine":3,"endLine":3,"children":[]},{"type":"heading","start":121,"end":134,"startLine":5,"endLine":5,"children":[]},{"type":"paragraph","start":136,"end":208,"startLine":7,"endLine":7,"children":[]},{"type":"paragraph","start":210,"end":451,"startLine":9,"endLine":9,"children":[]},{"type":"heading","start":453,"end":468,"startLine":11,"endLine":11,"children":[]},{"type":"paragraph","start":470,"end":649,"startLine":13,"endLine":13,"children":[]},{"type":"paragraph","start":651,"end":1211,"startLine":15,"endLine":15,"children":[]},{"type":"heading","start":1213,"end":1229,"startLine":17,"endLine":17,"children":[]},{"type":"paragraph","start":1231,"end":1309,"startLine":19,"endLine":19,"children":[]},{"type":"paragraph","start":1311,"end":1533,"startLine":21,"endLine":21,"children":[]},{"type":"paragraph","start":1535,"end":1721,"startLine":23,"endLine":23,"children":[]},{"type":"paragraph","start":1723,"end":1908,"startLine":25,"endLine":2